Definitive answer on the feeds — `AppState.swift:997-1009`:

```swift
if hasFDA     && !screenTimeDisabled { caps["screentime"] = true }
if hasPhotos  && !photosDisabled     { caps["photos"]     = true }
if hasCalendar && !calendarDisabled  { caps["calendar"]   = true }
```

Capabilities are gated on **macOS permissions**, and your MacBook is missing exactly the three that are paused. Screen Time needs **Full Disk Access**; Photos needs **Photos library access**. I set the schedules (those stuck), but `device-reconcile` re-pauses the status within seconds because the device says it can't serve them. This isn't something I can fix from the server — and I shouldn't, since the server is correctly following the device.

**One sequencing warning before you grant them:** you're running the agent's unsigned `99.0.0-dev` build. macOS ties permission grants to the code signature, so grants made now may not carry over to a signed release. Swap the real build in first, then grant. Once granted, the feeds re-activate on their own — no action needed from me.

Now merging, in the order my note prescribes.

